---
import Entry from '../../layouts/Entry.astro';
import CharityFinancialSearch from '../../components/CharityFinancialSearch.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/site';
import manifest from '../../../public/data/charity-financials/manifest.json';

const title = 'Charity financial filings';
const count = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const sources = manifest.sources.map(source => ({
  title: `${source.year} Annual Information Statement explanatory notes`,
  publisher: 'Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission', url: source.notes,
}));
---

<Entry title={title} eyebrow="The Record · Global Charity Index" summary="Read charity revenue, spending and grants alongside their fiscal periods and original sources." crumbs={[{label:'The Record',href:'/record/'},{label:'Global Charity Index',href:'/record/charity-index/'},{label:title}]} sources={sources}>
  <p>This edition covers {count(manifest.organizations)} Australian organizations with dated financial reporting in the 2023 or 2024 Annual Information Statement extracts. {count(manifest.organizationsWithBothYears)} have a dated record in both. The <a href={url('/observations/')}>separate historical financial panels</a> cover two consolidated reporting groups with U.S. parent identities.</p>
  <CharityFinancialSearch />
  <h2 id="coverage">Coverage and original data</h2>
  <p>Charitology retrieved these extracts on <time datetime={manifest.date}>{manifest.date}</time>. The statement year is the source’s label. The dates on each result show the reporting period. Amounts stay in Australian dollars and are shown as recorded, including reported zeroes. The 2024 extract supplies the displayed name.</p>
  <ul>{manifest.sources.map(source => <li>
    <strong>AIS {source.year}.</strong> {count(source.includedPeriods)} dated records included from {count(source.inputRows)} source records.
    {' '}{count(source.undated)} matched records lacked a complete reporting period.
    {source.olderOnly > 0 && ` ${count(source.olderOnly)} older records lacked a matching ABN in the 2024 extract.`}
    {source.duplicateRows > 0 && ` ${count(source.duplicateRows)} duplicate projection was collapsed.`}
    {' '}<a href={source.dataset}>Dataset</a> · <a href={source.csv}>Original CSV</a> · <a href={source.notes}>Field definitions</a>.
  </li>)}</ul>
  <p>Source: Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission. <a href={manifest.license}>Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Australia</a>. Charitology selected columns, converted date formats and linked statements by exact ABN. Some records are withheld by the regulator. Check the <a href="https://www.acnc.gov.au/charity/charities">current ACNC register</a> for current status and corrected information.</p>
  <p><a href={url('/data/charity-financials/manifest.json')} download>Download the coverage and source manifest</a> · <a href={url(`/data/charity-financials/${manifest.asset.path}`)} download>Download the full snapshot as compressed JSON</a>. The manifest gives the field order and original file fingerprints. Import ABNs as text when opening an export in a spreadsheet.</p>
  <h2>Reading the figures</h2>
  <p>Grants and donations shown here are amounts the reporting organization reported making for use inside or outside Australia. The figures do not identify individual recipients or where services were delivered. Revenue from government is an incoming amount. An award, a transfer and a recorded expense can describe different stages of the same money.</p>
  <p>A consolidated statement may cover more than one entity. A blank consolidation field leaves that scope unknown. Avoid adding figures across organizations because groups can overlap. A financial report describes money and its accounting scope. Evidence about what happened to people or communities comes from other sources.</p>
</Entry>
